      "confidence": 0.7,
      "curator_note": "Lower branch off the ring-opened distonic ion, labelled 'alpha': a genuine radical-site alpha-cleavage. The tail radical forms a new C=C pi bond (expelling neutral ethylene, C2H4, for Y=O) and the sigma bond beta to the radical breaks, leaving a radical on the carbon adjacent to Y. The product is the resonance-stabilised distonic oxonium/methylene ion .CH2-Y+=CH2 <-> CH2=Y+-CH2. (m/z 44 for Y=O). Book draws 0 electron-pushing fishhooks on this branch (only the 'alpha'-labelled reaction arrow); the two structures the book shows for the product ARE the two resonance forms, connected by a double-headed resonance arrow (eq 8.50). RESONANCE CHOICE (convention C): the mapped_smiles encodes the left/form-1 localisation .CH2(map5)-O+=CH2(map2); the right/form-2 CH2=O+-CH2.(map5) is the drawn resonance partner. The 3 fishhooks are curator-supplied for balance and reproduce standard radical-site alpha-cleavage exactly."
    },
